  "body": "## Brief/Intro/Overview\nThe `Router.sol` contract allows users to perform swaps but fails to accept or validate a transaction expiration timestamp (`deadline`). Unlike standard AMM Routers (e.g., Uniswap), which enforce that a transaction must execute by a specific time, Ekubo's router allows signed transactions to remain valid indefinitely. This exposes users to delayed execution and predatory MEV extraction.\n\n## Affected Contracts / Files\n* `src/Router.sol`\n\n## Vulnerability Details\nIn the Ethereum Virtual Machine (EVM), signed transactions do not have an inherent expiration time; they remain valid in the mempool until their nonce is consumed. To mitigate this, standard DeFi protocols include a `deadline` parameter in their Router functions, enforcing `require(block.timestamp <= deadline)`.\n\nThe `Router.sol` contract implements `swap`, `multihopSwap`, and `multiMultihopSwap` functions without this parameter or any equivalent check.\n\n**The Vulnerability:**\n1.  A user signs a transaction to swap `1 ETH` for `Token A` with a specific slippage tolerance.\n2.  The transaction to remain pending in the mempool (this could be intentionally or not).\n3.  Without a deadline, this transaction remains valid **indefinitely** (hours, days, or years).\n4.  A validator or MEV bot can \"hold\" this transaction and execute it at a future block where market conditions have changed drastically, often to the user's detriment.\n\n## Impact Details\n\n- **MEV Exploitation (The \"Free Option\"):** Without a deadline, a user's transaction gives validators a \"free option.\" They can hold the transaction and execute it **if and only if** it becomes profitable for them (e.g., waiting for market volatility to create a sandwiching opportunity). If it never becomes profitable, they drop it.\n\n- **Loss of User Agency:** Users lose the ability to safeguard their trades against time-based risks. A transaction intended for specific market conditions can execute long after those conditions have passed (e.g., after a stablecoin de-peg event).\n\n## Recommended Mitigation\n\nUpdate `Router.sol` (and all swap entry points) to accept a `uint256 deadline` parameter and enforce it using a modifier.\n\n## References\n\n- `src/Router.sol`: `swap`, `multihopSwap`, `multiMultihopSwap` functions.",
  "proof_of_concept": "## Proof of Concept\nThe following Foundry test demonstrates that a swap transaction created by a user can be executed successfully **1 year** after it was intended, confirming the absence of any time-validity checks.\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\npragma solidity >=0.8.30;\n\nimport {Test} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {Core} from \"../src/Core.sol\";\nimport {Router} from \"../src/Router.sol\";\nimport {Positions} from \"../src/Positions.sol\";\nimport {PoolKey} from \"../src/types/poolKey.sol\";\nimport {createFullRangePoolConfig} from \"../src/types/poolConfig.sol\";\nimport {\n    NATIVE_TOKEN_ADDRESS,\n    MIN_TICK,\n    MAX_TICK\n} from \"../src/math/constants.sol\";\nimport {SqrtRatio} from \"../src/types/sqrtRatio.sol\";\nimport {\n    SwapParameters,\n    createSwapParameters\n} from \"../src/types/swapParameters.sol\";\nimport {TestToken} from \"./TestToken.sol\";\nimport {console} from \"forge-std/console.sol\";\n\ncontract MissingDeadlineTest is Test {\n    Core core;\n    Router router;\n    Positions positions;\n    TestToken token1;\n    PoolKey poolKey;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        core = new Core();\n        router = new Router(core);\n        positions = new Positions(core, address(this), 0, 1);\n        token1 = new TestToken(address(this));\n\n        poolKey = PoolKey({\n            token0: NATIVE_TOKEN_ADDRESS,\n            token1: address(token1),\n            config: createFullRangePoolConfig(0, address(0))\n        });\n\n        core.initializePool(poolKey, 0);\n\n        // Add Liquidity to make swapping possible\n        token1.approve(address(positions), type(uint256).max);\n        positions.mintAndDeposit{value: 1000 ether}(\n            poolKey,\n            MIN_TICK,\n            MAX_TICK,\n            1000 ether,\n            1000 ether,\n            0\n        );\n    }\n\n    function test_swap_transaction_never_expires() public {\n        // 1. SETUP: User prepares a swap\n        address user = makeAddr(\"user\");\n        vm.deal(user, 10 ether);\n\n        // Snapshot the time when the transaction is \"signed/created\"\n        uint256 transactionCreationTime = vm.getBlockTimestamp();\n\n        int128 swapAmount = 1 ether;\n        SwapParameters params = createSwapParameters({\n            _amount: swapAmount,\n            _isToken1: false,\n            _sqrtRatioLimit: SqrtRatio.wrap(0),\n            _skipAhead: 0\n        });\n\n        // 2. Validator/MEV Bot holds the transaction\n        // We warp time forward by 1 year\n        uint256 executionTime = transactionCreationTime + 365 days;\n        vm.warp(executionTime);\n\n        console.log(\"Tx Created at:\", transactionCreationTime);\n        console.log(\"Tx Executed at:\", block.timestamp);\n        console.log(\n            \"Time Delay:\",\n            block.timestamp - transactionCreationTime,\n            \"seconds\"\n        );\n\n        // 3. EXECUTION\n        vm.prank(user);\n        router.swap{value: 1 ether}(poolKey, params, type(int256).min, user);\n\n        // 4. ASSERTION\n        uint256 userTokenBalance = token1.balanceOf(user);\n        console.log(\"User received tokens:\", userTokenBalance);\n\n        assertGt(\n            userTokenBalance,\n            0,\n            \"Swap succeeded (VULNERABLE): Should have reverted due to expiration\"\n        );\n        assertEq(address(user).balance, 9 ether, \"User spent ETH\");\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Run the Code**: `forge test --match-path test/MissingDeadline.t.sol`\n**Expected Output**: \n```bash\nRan 1 test for test/MissingDeadline.t.sol:MissingDeadlineTest\n[PASS] test_swap_transaction_never_expires() (gas: 92541)\nLogs:\n  Tx Created at: 1\n  Tx Executed at: 31536001\n  Time Delay: 31536000 seconds\n  User received tokens: 999000999000999000\n\nSuite result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 6.38ms (2.93ms CPU time)\n\nRan 1 test suite in 46.70ms (6.38ms CPU time): 1 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (1 total tests)\n```",
